"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cx2zrrpkx20o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The revelations in Anthropic's threat intelligence report come after a former top researcher at the company warned of the risks of AI to humanity.</summary></entry><entry><title>Can Europe recharge its battery industry?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjeg8ly0qd3o#0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T23:05:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjeg8ly0qd3o--994e2667a399.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjeg8ly0qd3o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Europe has some promising battery tech, but can it make up ground lost to Chinese battery giants?</summary></entry><entry><title>UK needs new laws for AI in healthcare, says watchdog</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3wjn3pl63xo#0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T00:48:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3wjn3pl63xo--1c6ce2d83174.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3wjn3pl63xo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The technology will soon be routinely used within the NHS, MHRA chief Lawrence Tallon tells the BBC.</summary></entry><entry><title>Google picks Finland for its largest single investment in Europe</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8r6y4me2g6o#0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:06:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8r6y4me2g6o--46858d52b764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8r6y4me2g6o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The US tech giant says the €13bn data centre project will create tens of thousands of jobs.</summary></entry><entry><title>Anthropic researcher believes more than 10% chance AI 'could kill all humans'</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckgwy1k42w4o#0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:34:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckgwy1k42w4o--9e44e55034b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckgwy1k42w4o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">It is the latest in a series of increasing warnings about the safety threat posed by artificial intelligence.</summary></entry><entry><title>White House pulls Tetris-style 'Build The Wall' game after copyright concern</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9v9djj4m3do#0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:06:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9v9djj4m3do--561a5d593b7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9v9djj4m3do?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The Tetris Company says it takes "copyright infringement very seriously" and is not involved with the game.</summary></entry><entry><title>Meta continues to run ads promoting child sexual abuse material in India - report</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqxv2vwjjq3o#0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T23:27:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqxv2vwjjq3o--d39fb1c8e98b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqxv2vwjjq3o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The report follows a BBC Eye investigation that found Instagram running paid ads promoting such material in India.</summary></entry><entry><title>Should promotion depend on how workers use AI?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1j1896e973o#0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T23:05:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1j1896e973o--ad6c061b96f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1j1896e973o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">More companies are tying career progression to AI use: is that fair?</summary></entry><entry><title>OpenAI says it cracked 90-year-old maths problem in 88 hours</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy7zygy3rl2o#0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T20:57:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy7zygy3rl2o--c539a0032086.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy7zygy3rl2o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">OpenAI's claim that it solved parts of Navier-Stokes equations has quickly stirred controversy.</summary></entry><entry><title>New law to force tech firms to stop children taking or sharing nude images</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgrv9ypp5x2o#0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:48:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgrv9ypp5x2o--6890aee9fa87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgrv9ypp5x2o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The government said it will legislate "as soon as they can" but may "reassess" its plans if firms make the desired changes sooner.</summary></entry><entry><title>Scammers demand ransoms from Instagram users over fake copyright claims</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjw54ww73qjo#0</id><updated>2026-09-11T19:12:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:49:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjw54ww73qjo-